cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use TERRA-X, please cite it as below, and cite the NASA, JPL and Copernicus
  datasets it is built on (listed under references and in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).
title: "TERRA-X: Earth analogs for lunar south pole operations"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-15
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/gadielvera12954/NASA-TERRAX
url: https://nasa-terrax.vercel.app
abstract: >-
  TERRA-X finds places on Earth where a crew can rehearse work planned for the lunar south
  pole (a VIPER-class rover at Mons Mouton, 84.60°S 31.00°E). It runs the same physics and the
  same 60 m grid on lunar relief (NASA LOLA) and on Earth relief (Copernicus DEM), with the Sun
  from JPL ephemerides, and reports for every candidate what transfers, what does not and what
  must be measured first. Built during the NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026, Ciudad del Este.
authors:
  - name: "TERRA-X team, NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026 (Ciudad del Este, Paraguay)"
keywords:
  - lunar south pole
  - terrestrial analogs
  - Mons Mouton
  - VIPER
  - LOLA
  - grazing sunlight
  - NASA Space Apps Challenge
